          "source_snippet": "\\begin{lemma}[Averaged defect in triangle inequality]\\label{tridef} Suppose that $\\zeta \\in D(z_0,r/2)$ and $\\zeta' \\in D(z_0, Cr)$ for some $z_0 \\in \\C$ and $C, r > 0$. Then $$ \\int_{D(z_0,r)} \\frac{1}{|z-\\zeta|} + \\frac{1}{|z-\\zeta'|} - \\left| \\frac{1}{z-\\zeta} + \\frac{1}{z-\\zeta'} \\right|\\ dA(z) \\asymp_C |\\zeta-\\zeta'|.$$ \\end{lemma}",
